  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>If the satellite was orbiting the Earth in a circular orbit of radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></math>, then its time period would be</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn mathvariant=\"normal\">2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>The same would be the time period of the satellite if it orbits in an ellipse having a&nbsp;semi-major axis&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></math></p><p>The area of the ellipse is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math>&nbsp;is the angular momentum of the satellite about the centre of the Earth.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msqrt><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mn>8</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math></p>",
